# SVG Assets → Svelte Icon Components

## Export rule

- Anything taken from a design tool (icons, logos, illustrations, decorative shapes) MUST first be attempted as **SVG**. Only fall back to raster (PNG/WebP) when the asset is inherently bitmap (photos, complex textures) or the tool refuses a vector export.
- NEVER hand-write or invent SVG paths — copy the exact markup from the SVG export.
- Do NOT save exported SVGs as `.svg` files in `static/assets/`. Static `.svg` files cannot change color across light/dark themes.

## Storage rule

Every exported SVG becomes a Svelte component:

- Location: `src/lib/icons/IconName.svelte` (PascalCase).
- Barrel export: append to `src/lib/icons/index.ts`: `export { default as IconName } from './IconName.svelte';`
- Keep the design-tool layer name as the component name when reasonable.

## Component template

Make color themeable with `currentColor` and accept a `class` prop:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  interface Props {
    class?: string;
  }

  let { class: className = '' }: Props = $props();
</script>

<svg
  class={className}
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <path d="..." stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
</svg>
```

## Requirements

1. Replace every themeable `fill="#hex"` / `stroke="#hex"` with `fill="currentColor"` / `stroke="currentColor"`. Keep a literal color only when it must NOT follow the theme (e.g. a fixed brand gradient).
2. Always forward `class` so callers can size and recolor: `<MoonOutline class="size-5 text-fg-3 dark:text-fg-1" />`.
3. No fixed `width`/`height` attributes — size via the `class` prop (`size-4`, `size-8`, ...). Keep `viewBox`.
4. Decorative icons get `aria-hidden="true"`; meaningful ones accept an optional `title` prop plus `role="img"` and `<title>`.
5. Keep the SVG geometry (paths, viewBox, `fill-rule`, gradients) exactly as exported — only adapt colors and attributes listed above.
6. Multi-color assets keep their internal colors; only the parts meant to follow the theme use `currentColor`.

## Usage

```svelte
import { MoonOutline } from '$lib/icons';

<MoonOutline class="size-5 text-fg-3 dark:text-fg-1" />
```

Theming via Tailwind color utilities + `dark:` variants on the class — never duplicate SVG files per theme.
